hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17338","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah, he said haddathana Hariz, he said I heard Sad ibn Marthad al-Rahabi, he said I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Hawshab narrating from Thawban ibn Shahr, he said I heard Kurayb ibn Abraha, while he was sitting with Abd al-Malik at Dayr al-Murran, and they mentioned pride, so Kurayb said: I heard Abu Rayhanah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Nothing of pride will enter Paradise. He said: Then one said: O Messenger of Allah, I like to beautify myself with the thong of my whip and the strap of my sandal. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not pride, Allah, Exalted is He, is Beautiful and loves beauty. Pride is only whoever rejects the truth and despises people with his eyes."
"17339","Haddathana Isam ibn Khalid, haddathana Hariz ibn Uthman, from Sad ibn Marthad al-Rahabi, he said I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Hawshab narrating from Thawban ibn Shahr al-Ashari, he said I heard Kurayb ibn Abraha, while he was sitting with Abd al-Malik upon his bed at Dayr al-Murran, and he mentioned pride, so Kurayb said: I heard Abu Rayhanah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Nothing of pride will enter Paradise. So one said: O Prophet of Allah, I like to beautify myself with the cords of my whip and the strap of my sandal. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not pride, Allah, Exalted is He, is Beautiful and loves beauty. Pride is only whoever rejects the truth and despises people with his eyes, meaning by the cords the strap of the whip and the thong of the sandal."
"17340","Haddathana Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, haddathana Layth, haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abi al-Husayn al-Himyari, from Abi Rayhanah, that he said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade teeth-filing, tattooing, plucking, secret marriage, intimate contact under one cover, continuous fasting, and touching without trade."
"17341","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, haddathana al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah, haddathani Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Abi al-Husayn al-Haytham ibn Shufay, that he heard him saying: I and a companion of mine called Abu Amir, a man of the Maafir, went out to pray in Iliya, and their storyteller was a man of the Azd called Abu Rayhanah, from the Companions. Abu al-Husayn said: My companion preceded me to the mosque, then I reached him and sat beside him, so he asked me: Did you catch the stories of Abu Rayhanah. I said: No. He said: I heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ten: teeth-filing, tattooing, plucking, and a man sleeping intimately with a man without a garment, and a woman sleeping intimately with a woman without a garment, and that a man put silk in the lower part of his garments like banners, and that he put upon his shoulders like the non-Arabs, and plunder, and riding leopards, and wearing a ring except for one with authority."
"17342","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, haddathani Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Himyari, from Abi Husayn al-Hajari, from Amir al-Hajari, from Abi Rayhanah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he disliked ten traits: teeth-filing, plucking, tattooing, a man sleeping intimately with a man and a woman with a woman with no garment between them, plunder, riding leopards, taking brocade here and here below in garments and upon shoulders, and a ring except for one with authority."
"17343","Haddathana al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab, he said haddathana Ibn Lahiah, he said haddathana Ayyash ibn Abbas, he said haddathani Abu al-Husayn, from Abi Rayhanah, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a ring except for one with authority."
"17344","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Humayd al-Kindi, from Ubadah ibn Nusay, from Abi Rayhanah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever claims descent to nine disbelieving forefathers, seeking by them honor and nobility, then he is the tenth of them in the Fire."
"17345","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, he said haddathani Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh, he said I heard Muhammad ibn Sumayr al-Ruayni saying: I heard Abu Amir al-Tujibi, my father said, and others than Zayd said: Abu Ali al-Janabi, meaning other than Zayd, Abu Ali al-Janabi, saying: I heard Abu Rayhanah saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a campaign, and we came one night to a height and spent the night upon it, and severe cold befell us until I saw one digging a pit in the ground, entering it, casting over it the shield, meaning the shield. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that from the people, he called: Who will guard us this night, and I will supplicate for him with a supplication in which is bounty. So a man from the Ansar said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Come near. So he came near. He said: Who are you. So the Ansari named himself to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with supplication and made much of it. Abu Rayhanah said: When I heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, I said: I am another man. He said: Come near. So I came near. He said: Who are you. He said: So I said: I am Abu Rayhanah. So he supplicated with a supplication less than what he supplicated for the Ansari. Then he said: The Fire is forbidden for an eye that shed tears or wept from fear of Allah, and the Fire is forbidden for an eye that kept watch in the path of Allah, or he said: The Fire is forbidden for another third eye, which Muhammad ibn Sumayr did not hear, and others said, meaning other than Zayd, Abu Ali al-Janabi."
"17346","Haddathana Attab, he said haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, he said haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh, akhbarani Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani, from Abi al-Husayn al-Hajari, that he informed him that he and a companion of his kept to Abu Rayhanah, learning good from him. He said: My companion attended one day and I did not attend, so my companion informed me that he heard Abu Rayhanah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ten: teeth-filing, tattooing, plucking, a man sleeping intimately with a man with no garment between them, and a woman with a woman with no garment between them, and two silk lines at the bottom of the garment, and two silk lines upon the shoulders, and the leopard, meaning leopard skin, and plunder, and a ring except for one with authority."
